**Sync protocol:**
```javascript
// Efficient sync after offline period
class YjsSyncProtocol {
  async sync(doc, remoteDoc) {
    // 1. Exchange state vectors (compact summary of what each peer has)
    const localState = Y.encodeStateVector(doc);
    const remoteState = Y.encodeStateVector(remoteDoc);

    // 2. Send only missing updates
    const missingLocal = Y.encodeStateAsUpdate(doc, remoteState);
    const missingRemote = Y.encodeStateAsUpdate(remoteDoc, localState);

    // 3. Apply updates
    Y.applyUpdate(doc, missingRemote);
    Y.applyUpdate(remoteDoc, missingLocal);

    // Guaranteed convergence
  }
}
```

**Real-world offline scenarios:**
```
Scenario 1: Brief disconnection (seconds to minutes)
- Changes queued in memory
- Automatic reconnection and sync
- User barely notices

Scenario 2: Extended offline (hours to days)
- Changes persisted to IndexedDB
- Document remains fully functional
- Sync on reconnection (typically <1 second for reasonable edits)

Scenario 3: Concurrent offline editing
- Multiple users edit offline
- All come online at different times
- All changes merge correctly
- No data loss
```

